        "source": "Hydrogen peroxide absorbs at 3.5 um on Europa (Trumbo, Brown & Hand 2019, AJ 158, 127, doi:10.3847/1538-3881/ab380c), and Wu, Trumbo, Brown & de Kleer (2024, PSJ, doi:10.3847/PSJ/ad7468) map it in these JWST cubes. Both remove a second-order polynomial fitted over 3.37-3.715 um with 3.4-3.65 um excluded, which this record's straight-line continuum cannot reproduce; the band and continuum windows here are this repository's, set narrowly either side of the 3.50 um core, so the depth is not comparable with the published band area."
